  {
   "id": "B",
   "title": "sp · st · -e · -er · -ig · -tion · pf",
   "said": [
    "p.spreche",
    "v.studieren",
    "n.strasse",
    "n.frage",
    "a.richtig",
    "n.apfel"
   ],
   "steps": [
    {
     "type": "video",
     "title": "Video: letter combinations (part 2)",
     "videoId": "nI77g2VWysE",
     "channel": "YourGermanTeacher (Johannes)",
     "start": 417,
     "end": 895,
     "note": "Chapters: 6:57 **sp / st** · 9:50 **-e / -er** · 10:47 **-ig** · 11:43 **-tion** · 12:17 **pf** · 13:05 bonus tips (chs, ch at the start)."
    },
    {
     "type": "compare",
     "title": "Combinations vs English",
     "items": [
      {
       "letter": "sp-",
       "example": "Ich spreche Deutsch.",
       "en": "shp — like “sh” + “p”",
       "mouth": "Only at the **start** of a word (or word part): *sprechen, Spanien, Beispiel, spielen*."
      },
      {
       "letter": "st-",
       "example": "die Straße",
       "en": "sht — like “sh” + “t”",
       "mouth": "At the start: *studieren, Straße, aufstehen*. At the **end** it is a normal *s* + *t*: *Obst, fast, kosten*."
      },
      {
       "letter": "-e",
       "example": "die Frage",
       "mouth": "A final *e* is **always pronounced** — a short, relaxed “uh”: *Frage, leise, Lampe*.",
       "en": "ə — like the “a” in “sofa” / “about”"
      },
      {
       "letter": "-er",
       "example": "der Vater",
       "mouth": "Final *-er* sounds like a short, open *a* — the *r* is not rolled: *besser, super, Vater*.",
       "en": "like the end of British “butter” (no r)"
      },
      {
       "letter": "-ig",
       "example": "richtig",
       "none": true,
       "mouth": "Two accepted ways: *-ich* (standard, with the soft *ch* from *ich*) or *-ik* (south). *richtig, König, vierzig*."
      },
      {
       "letter": "-tion",
       "example": "die Station",
       "en": "ts — as in “cats”",
       "mouth": "*-tion* = *ts* + *i-ohn* (“tsi-OHN”). Never English “shun”! *Station, Position, funktionieren*."
      },
      {
       "letter": "pf",
       "example": "der Apfel",
       "none": true,
       "mouth": "Say **both** sounds quickly: lips closed for *p*, then open into *f*. *Pferd, Apfel*."
      },
      {
